Eth. GYRISOENI (Eth. *gurisoi/noi), a people of Hispania Baetica, in the
                        neighbourhood of Castulo. (Plut. Sert. 3;
                        Ukert, vol. ii. pt. 1. p. 410.)

In these we have the measure of his operations. They were undoubtedly great;
                        though not greater than those of Alaric, and Genseric, and other conquerors
