TMOLUS a town of Lydia, situated on Mount Tmolus,
                        which was destroyed during the great earthquake in A.D. 19. (Tac. Ann. 2.47; Plin. Nat. 5.30; Euseb. Chron. ad Ann. V. Tib.;
                        Niceph. Call. 1.17.) Some coins are extant with the inscription *tmwlei/twn. (Sestini, p. 114.)

TRALLICON a town of Caria, mentioned only by Pliny
                            (5.29), situated on the river Harpasus;
                        but in his time it had already ceased to exist.

