USPE a town of the Siraci in Sarmatia, lying E. of
                        the Tanais. It lay on a height, and was fortified with a ditch and walls;
                        but the latter were composed only of mud confined in hurdles. (Tac. Ann. 12.16.)

ZIRINAE (Tab. Peut.;
                        *zeirini/a, Steph. B.
                            sub voce p. 287; Zernae, with various readings, in It.
                            Ant. p. 322), a town in Thrace, on the Hebrus, between Trajanopolis
